        "date": "2026-11-13T20:41:48Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui): edge picks are one edge per click, selected and hovered picks read strongly\n\nA plain or Ctrl click took the tangent chain (one edge, two, or a whole\nrounded outline by geometry alone); now it takes the edge under the\ncursor and only Shift takes the chain/loop. Ctrl+click on an edge a\nShift-taken pick already covers removes it instead of stacking. Selected\npicks draw 3 px with a dark halo, list-row hover 5 px; the row's remove\nbutton lights the pick too.\n\nFixes #1505\nFixes #1507\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
